{"step_index":196,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:38:39Z","content":"Here are the direct links to open the markdown artifacts in your Markdown preview:\n\n---\n\n### 📋 **1. Agile User Stories & Acceptance Criteria**\nClick to open in Markdown Preview:  \n👉 **[user_stories.md](file:///usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/user_stories.md)**\n\n* **Contents:** Complete sprint backlog, 21 user stories across 6 epics, story point estimates (Fibonacci scale), detailed technical implementation specifications, and formal **Gherkin (`Given-When-Then`)** acceptance criteria for all flows and edge cases.\n\n---\n\n### 📊 **2. Visual Architecture & Workflow Diagrams (Mermaid)**\nClick to open in Markdown Preview:  \n👉 **[architecture_diagrams.md](file:///usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/architecture_diagrams.md)**\n\n* **Contents:** End-to-end C4 container system topology, Policy RAG query sequence flow, Leave Booking with Human-in-the-Loop confirmation flow, Medical Leave with Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ) sequence flow, ServiceImmediately and WorkWeek lifecycle state machines, and the 5-stage Security & Safety processing pipeline.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 **3. Combined Technical Specifications & User Stories**\nClick to open in Markdown Preview:  \n👉 **[specs_and_user_stories.md](file:///usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/specs_and_user_stories.md)**\n\n* **Contents:** Complete engineering technical specifications, `X-Authenticated-User` signed JWT contracts, `Idempotency-Key` protocols, API error envelopes, sequence diagrams, and user stories."}
