{"step_index":199,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:40:37Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-17T14:40:37Z\nCompleted At: 2026-08-17T14:40:38Z\nSkill search results:\n- gdrive (/google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3/learning/gemini/agents/skills/gdrive/SKILL.md): List, search, upload, download, update, and manage Google Drive files and folders using a Go CLI. Use when listing files, searching Drive, downloading or uploading files, updating file content in-place, creating folders, creating shortcuts, moving/copying/renaming files, sharing, managing permissions, viewing revisions, exporting Google files, getting file URLs, or monitoring and watching Drive activity for triggers. Don't use for editing Docs/Sheets/Slides content (use those specific skills instead). Also use when the user shares a drive.google.com URL.\n- gslides (/google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3/learning/gemini/agents/skills/gslides/SKILL.md): Read, create, and edit Google Slides presentations using a Go CLI. Use when reading slide content, creating presentations, adding/duplicating/reordering slides, adding text boxes, images, tables, setting backgrounds, managing speaker notes, exporting to PDF/PPTX, or extracting images. Also use when the user shares a slides.google.com URL. Don't use for Google Docs, Sheets, or Drive file management.\n- google3 (/google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3/learning/gemini/agents/skills/google3/SKILL.md): Explains how to read, search (Code Search), modify (CitC workspaces), run presubmits, and commit (Critique) source code in Google3, Google's internal codebase. Use when navigating Google3 paths, performing Code Search queries, working with CitC workspaces, running presubmit checks, or managing Piper CLs. Don't use for Git-only workspaces or non-Piper source control systems.\n- vcs (/google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3/learning/gemini/agents/skills/vcs/SKILL.md): Manage version control in Google3/Piper workspaces using Fig (hg), jj (Jujutsu), or Piper (g4). Covers workspace setup, commits, CL lifecycle (upload, mail, submit), splitting, rebasing, conflict resolution, and Critique integration. Use when the user works with source control, CLs, changelists, commits, diffs, uploads, code review, syncing, or repository operations in Google3. MUST READ before running any VCS operations. Don't use for non-Piper version control systems, Git-only workspaces, generic GitHub/GitLab repositories outside of Google3, or tasks unrelated to source control.\n- google-workspace (/google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3/learning/gemini/agents/skills/google_workspace/SKILL.md): Access Google Workspace (Docs, Sheets, Slides, Drive, Calendar, Gmail, Chat, Keep). Use for reading docs.google.com URLs, searching emails/calendar, downloading/creating files, and semantic search across Workspace corpora.\n- filesystems (/google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3/learning/gemini/agents/skills/filesystems/SKILL.md): Covers how to read or manage files for internal Google filesystems: /cns/, /x20/, /tfhub/, /google_src/. Explains how to use `fileutil` from the command line and the `gfile` API from code. A **MUST READ** before accessing any of these filesystems.\n- drive_folders (/google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3/apps/intelligence/gen_ai/control_plane/shared/skills_repository/skills/drive_folders/1/SKILL.md): Use when creating folders, setting up project directory structures, or moving files into folders in Google Drive. Don't use for searching Drive files, reading document contents, downloading files, or editing Google Docs, Sheets, or Slides content.\n- drive-folders (/google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3/apps/intelligence/gen_ai/control_plane/shared/skills_repository/skills/drive_folders/experimental_mcp/SKILL.md): Use when creating folders, setting up project directory structures, or moving files into folders in Google Drive. Don't use for searching Drive files, reading document contents, downloading files, or editing Google Docs, Sheets, or Slides content.\n- drive_folders (/google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3/learning/agents/orcas/chiliagon/agents/sobi/skills/google-drive/SKILL.md): Use when creating folders, setting up project directory structures, or moving files into folders in Google Drive. Don't use for searching Drive files, reading document contents, downloading files, or editing Google Docs, Sheets, or Slides content.\n- capsule (/google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3/learning/gemini/agents/skills/capsule/SKILL.md): How to provision, access, and use Google-internal dedicated environments for agents called Capsules. Covers spawning capsules, SSH access, troubleshooting rshell logs (go/rshell, go/rshelld, go/cpl-cli) with f1-sql, and analyzing startup time with systemd-analyze."}
