{"step_index":201,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:40:40Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-17T14:40:40Z\nCompleted At: 2026-08-17T14:40:40Z\nFile Path: `file:///google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3/learning/gemini/agents/skills/gdrive/SKILL.md`\nTotal Lines: 253\nTotal Bytes: 12088\nShowing lines 1 to 253\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: name: gdrive\n3: description: >-\n4:     List, search, upload, download, update, and manage Google Drive files and\n5:     folders using a Go CLI. Use when listing files, searching Drive, downloading\n6:     or uploading files, updating file content in-place, creating folders,\n7:     creating shortcuts, moving/copying/renaming files, sharing, managing permissions, viewing\n8:     revisions, exporting Google files, getting file URLs, or monitoring and\n9:     watching Drive activity for triggers. Don't use for editing\n10:     Docs/Sheets/Slides content (use those specific skills instead). Also use\n11:     when the user shares a drive.google.com URL.\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # gdrive\n15: \n16: ## Command Namespacing & Security\n17: \n18: To enforce robust agent safety boundaries and support prefix-based terminal\n19: command permission scopes, the `gdrive` CLI routes operations through dedicated\n20: `readonly` and `mutate` namespaces:\n21: \n22: -   **`readonly` namespace**: Applied to commands that strictly browse, search,\n23:     read, export, or audit Drive assets without modifying any remote state.\n24: -   **`mutate` namespace**: Applied to commands that upload files, edit content,\n25:     create folders, delete files, or manage sharing permissions in the cloud.\n26: \n27: AI agents MUST consistently use the namespaced subcommand structures shown below\n28: (e.g. `gdrive readonly ls` and `gdrive mutate upload`).\n29: \n30: -   **CXF-Delegated Impersonation**: Pass the global flag `--target_user <ldap>`\n31:     to act on behalf of another user. The CLI automatically requests the\n32:     narrowest required OAuth scope list (e.g. `drive.metadata.readonly`, etc.)\n33:     rather than the full `drive` scope whenever possible to satisfy the target\n34:     user's minimal privilege principles.\n35: \n36: > [!CAUTION]\n37: >\n38: > The `empty-trash` and `delete` commands permanently remove files and cannot be\n39: > undone. **Never** use destructive commands unless the user explicitly asks.\n40: \n41: ## CLI\n42: \n43: Prefer using the pre-built binary (available on all gLinux machines):\n44: \n45: ```bash\n46: GDRIVE=/google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdrive/gdrive\n47: ```\n48: \n49: Alternatively, install via apt (the `gdrive` binary will be available directly\n50: on PATH):\n51: \n52: ```bash\n53: sudo glinux-add-repo -b gemini-agents-gdrive stable\n54: sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y gemini-agents-gdrive\n55: ```\n56: \n57: If you need to build from source:\n58: \n59: ```bash\n60: blaze build //learning/gemini/agents/clis/gdrive:gdrive\n61: GDRIVE=blaze-bin/learning/gemini/agents/clis/gdrive/gdrive\n62: ```\n63: \n64: > [!CAUTION]\n65: >\n66: > The `empty-trash` command permanently deletes **all** trashed files and cannot\n67: > be undone. Only run it with explicit user approval.\n68: \n69: > [!IMPORTANT]\n70: >\n71: > **Efficiency Guidelines**:\n72: >\n73: > -   Answer general or conceptual questions about Drive commands (e.g., \"Is\n74: >     empty-trash reversible?\") directly using the details in this `SKILL.md`\n75: >     file.\n76: >\n77: > -   Do **NOT** call tools (e.g., `code_search`, `view_file`, `list_dir`) to\n78: >     inspect source code or documentation unless the prompt specifically asks\n79: >     to inspect file content or implementation details.\n80: >\n81: > -   **Ignore Workspace Context**: Ignore workspace-specific context (e.g.,\n82: >     CitC workspace name, pending changes, CL numbers in path) when answering.\n83: >     Focus solely on the prompt.\n84: \n85: ## Recipes\n86: \n87: **Browse and search:**\n88: \n89: ```bash\n90: $GDRIVE readonly ls                                # list root\n91: $GDRIVE readonly ls FOLDER_ID --max 50\n92: $GDRIVE readonly ls --trashed                      # list trashed items\n93: $GDRIVE readonly search --name-contains \"quarterly report\"\n94: $GDRIVE readonly search --content-contains \"annual budget\" # search text within file content\n95: $GDRIVE readonly search --parent-id FOLDER_ID --modified-after 2024-01-01T00:00:00Z --type spreadsheet\n96: $GDRIVE readonly search --name-contains \"quarterly report\" --include-trashed # search trashed items\n97: $GDRIVE readonly recent --max 10\n98: $GDRIVE readonly starred\n99: $GDRIVE readonly info FILE_ID\n100: $GDRIVE readonly capabilities FILE_ID\n101: $GDRIVE readonly capabilities FILE_ID --filter canEdit,canComment # filter specific capabilities to save tokens\n102: $GDRIVE readonly url FILE_ID                       # print web URL\n103: $GDRIVE readonly tree FOLDER_ID                    # recursive folder tree\n104: $GDRIVE readonly count FOLDER_ID                   # count items in folder with pagination\n105: ```\n106: \n107: **Exact Name Matching for Native Files:** Omit file extensions when searching\n108: for native Google Workspace files (Docs, Sheets, Slides) via exact match.\n109: Execute `$GDRIVE readonly search --name-exact \"Q3 Budget\"` instead of appending\n110: artificial extensions like `\"Q3 Budget.gsheet\"`. Include extensions only when\n111: searching exact names of binary uploads (e.g., `report.pdf`).\n112: \n113: **MIME Type Override on Upload and Update:** Bypass extension-based MIME type\n114: auto-detection by specifying `--mime-type`. This is critical for files like\n115: `.ipynb` that must be registered in Drive as Colab notebooks\n116: (`application/vnd.google.colaboratory` or\n117: `application/vnd.google.colaboratory.corp`) rather than generic notebooks\n118: (`application/x-ipynb+json`). This ensures they render as Colab notebooks and\n119: resolve correctly when referenced on other Google platforms.\n120: \n121: **Capabilities Filtering:** Use the `--filter` flag with `readonly capabilities`\n122: to retrieve only specific capabilities, which helps save context tokens. Common\n123: capabilities include `canEdit`, `canComment`, and `canShare`.For a full list of\n124: available capabilities, see the\n125: [Google Drive API Files Resource](https://developers.google.com/workspace/drive/api/reference/rest/v3/files#resource:-file).\n126: \n127: **File operations:**\n128: \n129: ```bash\n130: $GDRIVE readonly download FILE_ID --out /tmp/file.pdf\n131: $GDRIVE mutate upload /tmp/file.txt --parent FOLDER_ID\n132: $GDRIVE mutate upload /tmp/notebook.ipynb --mime-type \"application/vnd.google.colaboratory\" --parent FOLDER_ID  # upload with custom MIME type (e.g. Colab)\n133: $GDRIVE mutate update FILE_ID /tmp/updated_notebook.ipynb  # replace content, keep ID/link/permissions\n134: $GDRIVE mutate update FILE_ID /tmp/updated_notebook.ipynb --mime-type \"application/vnd.google.colaboratory\"  # update content and set MIME type\n135: $GDRIVE mutate mkdir \"New Folder\" --parent FOLDER_ID\n136: $GDRIVE mutate create-shortcut FILE_ID FOLDER_ID  # shortcut inherits original file name\n137: $GDRIVE mutate cp FILE_ID \"Copy of File\"\n138: $GDRIVE mutate mv FILE_ID NEW_PARENT_ID\n139: $GDRIVE mutate rename FILE_ID \"New Name\"\n140: $GDRIVE readonly export FILE_ID /tmp/doc.pdf --format pdf   # export Google files\n141: $GDRIVE mutate trash FILE_ID\n142: $GDRIVE mutate untrash FILE_ID\n143: $GDRIVE mutate empty-trash --confirm\n144: ```\n145: \n146: **Sharing and permissions:**\n147: \n148: > [!WARNING] The `share` command supports `--type anyone` which makes files\n149: > world-readable. Exercise extreme caution when using this flag to avoid\n150: > accidentally exposing sensitive files.\n151: \n152: ```bash\n153: $GDRIVE mutate share FILE_ID --email user@google.com --role writer\n154: $GDRIVE mutate share FILE_ID --email user@google.com --role reader --notify=false\n155: $GDRIVE readonly permissions FILE_ID\n156: $GDRIVE mutate remove-permission FILE_ID PERMISSION_ID\n157: $GDRIVE readonly audit-permissions FOLDER_ID        # recursive permission audit\n158: ```\n159: \n160: **Other:**\n161: \n162: ```bash\n163: $GDRIVE readonly quota\n164: $GDRIVE readonly revisions FILE_ID\n165: $GDRIVE readonly shared-drives\n166: $GDRIVE readonly list-comments FILE_ID\n167: $GDRIVE mutate add-comment FILE_ID 'Nice work!'\n168: $GDRIVE mutate reply-comment FILE_ID COMMENT_ID \"Done\"\n169: $GDRIVE mutate resolve-comment FILE_ID COMMENT_ID \"Resolved.\"\n170: $GDRIVE mutate batch -f ops.json\n171: $GDRIVE readonly watch --watch_actions=commented,edited\n172: ```\n173: \n174: **Note on Comments:** For commands that require a `COMMENT_ID` (like replying or\n175: resolving), you must use the original **Thread ID**, not a Reply ID.\n176: \n177: **Background Watchers:** To run an event-driven background watcher that triggers\n178: an agent upon Drive activity (like comments, etc.), use the `readonly watch`\n179: command.\n180: \n181: By default, it uses `events` mode which leverages Workspace Events API (WES) and\n182: Pub/Sub for real-time notifications. This requires a configured GCP project\n183: (resolved automatically or via `--project_id`). If you encounter setup or\n184: permission issues, you can fall back to polling mode:\n185: \n186: ```bash\n187: $GDRIVE readonly watch --watch_mode=poll --watch_actions=commented,edited\n188: ```\n189: \n190: **Filtering by MIME Type:** To ensure your watcher only discovers and subscribes\n191: to relevant file types (and eliminates noise from unrelated Drive files), use\n192: the `--mime_type` flag to filter by MIME type or shorthand alias (`docs`,\n193: `sheets`, `slides`, `folder`, `colab`, `pdf`).\n194: \n195: ```bash\n196: $GDRIVE readonly watch --mime_type=docs --watch_actions=commented,edited\n197: $GDRIVE readonly watch --watch_mode=poll --mime_type=sheets --watch_actions=commented,edited\n198: ```\n199: \n200: ## Commands\n201: \n202: | Command                      | Description                                   |\n203: | ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n204: | `readonly ls`                | List files (supports `--trashed`)             |\n205: | `readonly count`             | Count files in folder with pagination         |\n206: | `readonly search`            | Search files (supports `--trashed`)           |\n207: | `readonly info`              | Get file info                                 |\n208: | `readonly url`               | Print web URL                                 |\n209: | `readonly download`          | Download file                                 |\n210: | `mutate upload`              | Upload file (supports `--mime-type`)          |\n211: | `mutate update`              | Update file content in-place (preserves ID,   |\n212: :                              : link, permissions; supports `--mime-type`)    :\n213: | `mutate mkdir`               | Create folder                                 |\n214: | `mutate create-shortcut`     | Create a shortcut to a file in a folder       |\n215: | `mutate cp`                  | Copy file                                     |\n216: | `mutate mv`                  | Move file                                     |\n217: | `mutate rename`              | Rename file                                   |\n218: | `readonly export`            | Export Google file                            |\n219: | `mutate trash`               | Trash file                                    |\n220: | `mutate untrash`             | Restore file                                  |\n221: | `mutate empty-trash`         | Empty trash                                   |\n222: | `mutate share`               | Share file (`--notify=false` to suppress      |\n223: :                              : email)                                        :\n224: | `readonly permissions`       | List permissions                              |\n225: | `mutate remove-permission`   | Remove permission                             |\n226: | `readonly audit-permissions` | Recursive permission audit                    |\n227: | `readonly capabilities`      | List file capabilities (supports `--filter`)  |\n228: | `readonly recent`            | Recent files                                  |\n229: | `readonly starred`           | Starred files                                 |\n230: | `readonly quota`             | Show quota                                    |\n231: | `readonly revisions`         | List file revisions                           |\n232: | `readonly shared-drives`     | List shared drives                            |\n233: | `readonly tree`              | Display folder tree                           |\n234: | `readonly list-comments`     | List comments                                 |\n235: | `mutate add-comment`         | Add a comment                                 |\n236: | `mutate reply-comment`       | Reply to a specific comment thread            |\n237: | `mutate resolve-comment`     | Resolve a comment thread                      |\n238: | `mutate batch`               | Execute batch ops                             |\n239: | `readonly watch`             | Start a background watcher for Drive activity |\n240: \n241: ## Global Flags\n242: \n243: -   `--json` — output as JSON (works with all read commands)\n244: -   `--target_user <ldap>` — Act on behalf of the specified target user using\n245:     CXF-delegated impersonation (requires ssoproxy and appropriate\n246:     authorizations)\n247: \n248: ## Reporting Issues\n249: \n250: Report bugs or improvements for this skill at\n251: [Agent Skill: gdrive](http://b/hotlists/8078139). See the `skill_issue` skill\n252: for instructions on filing and triaging skill bugs.\n253: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
