{"step_index":238,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:48:58Z","thinking":"**Initiating Design Documentation**\n\nI'm starting to create the `design.md` file. My objective is to produce a detailed System Design Document, suitable for production, while embodying the roles of both a Principal Systems Architect and a Principal PM. I will ensure thoroughness.\n\n\n**Defining System Structure**\n\nI've outlined the major sections for the System Design Document, focusing on the HR agentic solution's MVP 1. Specifically, I'm fleshing out the context and objectives, ensuring that architectural principles like Zero-Trust and Loose Coupling are clearly defined. I'm also mapping out the high-level architecture and component decomposition into layers: Client, Gateway, Core Agent Platform, Knowledge & Retrieval, Integration Adapters, and Resilience. I need to get started on the data architecture next.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Comprehensive System Design Document (design.md) for the HR Agentic Solution (MVP 1).","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# System Design Document: HR Agentic Solution (MVP 1)\n\n**Document Version:** 1.0.0  \n**Status:** Approved / Ready for Implementation  \n**Authors:** Principal Systems Architect & Principal Product Manager  \n**Target Release:** MVP 1.0 (Q3 2026)  \n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary & Design Principles\n\nThe **HR Agentic Solution** is an enterprise-grade virtual assistant platform designed to automate Tier-1 HR/IT policy inquiries and execute self-service transactional workflows across **WorkWeek (HCM)** and **ServiceImmediately (ITSM/HRSD)**.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    User([Employee]) --> UI[Web Chat UI]\n    UI --> Gateway[API Gateway & Auth Proxy]\n    Gateway --> Safety[Safety & Guardrails]\n    Safety --> Orchestrator[Agent Orchestrator]\n    Orchestrator --> RAG[(Policy Vector DB)]\n    Orchestrator --> WW[WorkWeek Adapter]\n    Orchestrator --> SI[ServiceImmediately Adapter]\n    Orchestrator --> DLQ[(HR Ops DLQ)]\n```\n\n### Core Architectural Principles\n\n1. **Zero-Trust Identity Assertion:** Even in the MVP 1 test-credential sandbox environment, all user turns are authenticated via an **API Gateway Mock Identity Assertion Layer** that injects a cryptographically signed JWT (`X-Authenticated-User`) to enforce strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).\n2. **Deterministic State Mutation via Human-in-the-Loop (HITL):** The autonomous LLM is strictly prohibited from mutating external backend state without rendering an interactive **Confirmation Card** for explicit user review and authorization.\n3. **Resilience & Forward SAGA Consistency:** Multi-system chained workflows avoid brittle two-phase rollbacks; instead, they preserve successful upstream state and route partial downstream failures to an **HR Operations Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ)** with transparent user notifications.\n4. **Defense-in-Depth AI Safety:** Input guardrails, domain containment, closed-domain RAG retrieval gating, and NER-based SPII masking guarantee $\\ge 99.5\\%$ safety precision/recall and 0% ungrounded policy hallucinations.\n\n---\n\n## 2. High-Level System Architecture\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph Client_Tier [\"1. Client Ingress Tier\"]\n        Browser[\"Employee Browser\"]\n        ChatUI[\"React Web Chat UI\\n(SSE Token Streaming / HITL Cards)\"]\n        PersonaSelector[\"Test Persona Selector\\n(Jane Doe / John Smith / Alice Brown)\"]\n        Browser --> PersonaSelector\n        Browser --> ChatUI\n    end\n\n    subgraph Edge_Gateway [\"2. Edge & Security Gateway\"]\n        APIGW[\"API Gateway (Envoy / Express Proxy)\\nRate Limiting & CORS\"]\n        AuthService[\"Mock Identity Assertion Service\\n(Signs JWT Claims)\"]\n        InputScanner[\"Input Guardrail Interceptor\\n(< 300ms Prompt Injection Scanner)\"]\n        \n        ChatUI -->|POST /api/v1/chat/message| APIGW\n        PersonaSelector -.->|Select Persona| AuthService\n        AuthService -->|Injects X-Authenticated-User| APIGW\n        APIGW --> InputScanner\n    end\n\n    subgraph Agent_Core [\"3. Core Agent Orchestration Platform\"]\n        SessionStore[(\"Redis Session Cache\\n(30m Inactivity TTL)\")]\n        OrchestratorEngine[\"Agent Orchestrator (LangGraph / Custom)\\nIntent Parser & Tool Router\"]\n        RBACEnforcer[\"Orchestration-Level RBAC\\n(caller_id == resource_owner_id)\"]\n        OutputScanner[\"Output Guardrail & PII Scrubber\\n(NER Masking & Grounding Gate)\"]\n        \n        InputScanner -->|Sanitized Prompt| OrchestratorEngine\n        OrchestratorEngine <--> SessionStore\n        OrchestratorEngine --> RBACEnforcer\n        OrchestratorEngine --> OutputScanner\n    end\n\n    subgraph Subsystems_Tier [\"4. Integration Adapters & Retrieval Services\"]\n        WWAdapter[\"WorkWeek HCM Adapter\\n(Circuit Breaker / Idempotent REST)\"]\n        SIAdapter[\"ServiceImmediately Adapter\\n(15m Deduplication / Status Engine)\"]\n        RAGService[\"Policy RAG Retrieval Service\\n(Cosine Similarity, k=4, >= 0.70)\"]\n        \n        RBACEnforcer -->|Authorized Dispatch| WWAdapter\n        RBACEnforcer -->|Authorized Dispatch| SIAdapter\n        RBACEnforcer -->|Authorized Dispatch| RAGService\n    end\n\n    subgraph Data_Storage [\"5. Enterprise Backends & Persistence\"]\n        WorkWeekSandbox[(\"WorkWeek HCM Sandbox\\n(Profile & Balances)\")]\n        SISandbox[(\"ServiceImmediately Sandbox\\n(Incidents & HRSD)\")]\n        VectorStore[(\"Policy Vector Database\\n(Milvus / Pinecone / Cloud Vector)\")]\n        AuditDB[(\"PostgreSQL Audit Store\\n(PII-Masked Event Logs)\")]\n        DLQQueue[(\"Kafka / Cloud Pub/Sub\\n(HR Ops Dead-Letter Queue)\")]\n        \n        WWAdapter <-->|REST API| WorkWeekSandbox\n        SIAdapter <-->|REST API| SISandbox\n        RAGService <-->|Embedding Search| VectorStore\n        OrchestratorEngine -->|Async Event| AuditDB\n        OrchestratorEngine -.->|On Chained Step Failure| DLQQueue\n    end\n\n    OutputScanner -->|Streaming Clean SSE| ChatUI\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Deep Dive & Specifications\n\n### 3.1. API Gateway & Mock Identity Assertion\n* **Role:** Acts as the reverse proxy, TLS termination endpoint, rate limiter, and authenticated session provider.\n* **JWT Signing:** Signs an HMAC-SHA256 token containing caller context.\n* **Rate Limiting:** Enforces maximum 20 requests/minute per `session_id` to protect backend adapters from abuse.\n\n#### `X-Authenticated-User` JWT Payload Specification:\n```json\n{\n  \"sub\": \"EMP-1042\",\n  \"name\": \"Jane Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"jane.doe@enterprise.com\",\n  \"role\": \"employee\",\n  \"department\": \"Engineering\",\n  \"manager_id\": \"EMP-0088\",\n  \"location\": \"Remote\",\n  \"country\": \"US\",\n  \"iat\": 1723896000,\n  \"exp\": 1723903200\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3.2. Interaction Safety & Guardrails Interceptor\n* **Input Guardrail Engine:**\n  * Evaluates prompts against adversarial patterns (system prompt leakage, DAN jailbreaks, instruction overrides).\n  * Latency overhead budget: $< 300\\text{ms}$.\n  * Actions: Emits HTTP 400 with a polite refusal on violation and writes `SAFETY_INTERCEPT_INPUT` to the audit store.\n* **Output Guardrail & SPII Scrubber:**\n  * Uses Named Entity Recognition (NER) and regex pattern matching to mask SSNs, credit cards, bank accounts, personal phone numbers, and home addresses before saving to logs.\n  * Verifies grounding against retrieved RAG chunks to prevent policy hallucinations.\n\n---\n\n### 3.3. Agent Orchestrator & Multi-Turn State Manager\n* **Session Lifecycle:**\n  * State maintained in Redis using JSON data structures.\n  * Key format: `session:{session_id}:context`.\n  * TTL: 1800 seconds (30 minutes), refreshed on every incoming request.\n  * Reset Protocol: Command `/reset` deletes the key and restores initial persona state.\n* **Tool Dispatcher & RBAC:**\n  * Before invoking any adapter, the orchestrator inspects `X-Authenticated-User.sub`.\n  * Enforces invariant: `tool_payload.employee_id == X-Authenticated-User.sub`.\n\n---\n\n### 3.4. System Integration Adapters\n\n#### 1. WorkWeek HCM Adapter\n* **Operations:**\n  * `getProfile(employee_id)`: Fetches name, department, role, manager, address, phone.\n  * `getLeaveBalances(employee_id)`: Returns accrued, used, and remaining balances in **work days**.\n  * `submitLeave(payload)`: Validates business calendar (excluding weekends and corporate holidays), verifies `requested_days <= balance`, and submits request with status `SUBMITTED_FOR_APPROVAL`.\n  * `updateContactInfo(payload)`: Updates home address and E.164 phone number.\n* **Resilience Policy:**\n  * 5-second HTTP timeout.\n  * Exponential backoff with jitter (max 2 retries).\n  * Circuit breaker: 3 consecutive 5xx errors trip the breaker for 60 seconds.\n\n#### 2. ServiceImmediately ITSM/HRSD Adapter\n* **Operations:**\n  * `getTicket(ticket_id, caller_id)`: Retrieves status, priority, category, and comment timeline.\n  * `createIncident(payload)`: Maps intent to category (`Software/VPN`, `Hardware`, `Access`, `HR General`) and priority (`P1-P4`).\n  * `postComment(ticket_id, comment)`: Appends user notes to active tickets.\n  * `cancelTicket(ticket_id)`: Transitions ticket to `Canceled` only if current state is `New`.\n* **15-Minute Deduplication Engine:**\n  * Before ticket creation, queries open tickets created by `caller_id` within the last 15 minutes.\n  * Calculates semantic cosine distance on short descriptions. If similarity $> 0.85$, blocks creation and returns a prompt to the user to confirm or append a comment.\n\n#### 3. Policy Document RAG Retrieval Engine\n* **Vector Store Index:** Dense vector index with cosine similarity metric.\n* **Chunking Strategy:** 512 tokens with 50-token overlap; metadata indexed by `document_name`, `section_title`, `deep_link_url`, and `version_hash`.\n* **Retrieval Threshold:** Minimum cosine similarity $\\ge 0.70$. If top score $< 0.70$, triggers out-of-domain refusal prompt.\n* **Ingestion SLA:** $\\le 1\\text{ hour}$ via repository webhook / CDC pipeline, supported by manual `POST /api/v1/admin/rag/sync` and a nightly 24-hour full refresh cron.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Architecture & Database Schemas\n\n```mermaid\nerDiagram\n    AUDIT_EVENT {\n        string event_id PK\n        string trace_id\n        string session_id\n        string employee_id\n        string event_type\n        string action_name\n        jsonb request_payload_redacted\n        jsonb response_payload_redacted\n        string status\n        timestamp created_at\n    }\n\n    DLQ_EVENT {\n        string dlq_id PK\n        string trace_id\n        string employee_id\n        string workflow_name\n        string primary_ref_id\n        string failed_step\n        string error_message\n        int retry_count\n        string state\n        timestamp created_at\n    }\n\n    POLICY_DOCUMENT_INDEX {\n        string chunk_id PK\n        string document_name\n        string section_title\n        string deep_link_url\n        string document_hash\n        vector embedding_vector\n        text chunk_text\n        timestamp indexed_at\n    }\n\n    SESSION_STATE {\n        string session_id PK\n        string employee_id\n        jsonb message_history\n        jsonb pending_action\n        timestamp last_accessed_at\n    }\n```\n\n### 4.1. Audit Database Schema (PostgreSQL DDL)\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE audit_events (\n    event_id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    trace_id VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL,\n    session_id VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL,\n    employee_id VARCHAR(32) NOT NULL,\n    event_type VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL, -- 'TOOL_EXECUTION', 'SAFETY_INTERCEPT_INPUT', 'HITL_CONFIRM'\n    action_name VARCHAR(64),\n    target_system VARCHAR(64),       -- 'WorkWeek', 'ServiceImmediately', 'PolicyRAG'\n    request_payload_redacted JSONB,\n    response_payload_redacted JSONB,\n    status VARCHAR(32) NOT NULL,     -- 'SUCCESS', 'BLOCKED', 'FAILED', 'PARTIAL_SUCCESS'\n    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n);\n\nCREATE INDEX idx_audit_employee ON audit_events(employee_id);\nCREATE INDEX idx_audit_trace ON audit_events(trace_id);\nCREATE INDEX idx_audit_created ON audit_events(created_at);\n```\n\n### 4.2. Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ) Event Schema\n```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"HROps_DeadLetterQueue_Event\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\n    \"dlq_id\",\n    \"trace_id\",\n    \"employee_id\",\n    \"workflow_name\",\n    \"primary_ref_id\",\n    \"failed_step\",\n    \"error_details\",\n    \"timestamp\"\n  ],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"dlq_id\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"uuid\" },\n    \"trace_id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"employee_id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"workflow_name\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"UC-2.1-Procurement\", \"UC-2.2-MedicalLeave\"] },\n    \"primary_ref_id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"failed_step\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"error_details\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"http_status\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n        \"error_message\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"retry_attempts\": { \"type\": \"integer\" }\n      }\n    },\n    \"timestamp\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Sequence & Control Flow Specifications\n\n### 5.1. Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) State Mutation Flow\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Employee as Employee\n    participant UI as Web Chat UI\n    participant Gateway as API Gateway\n    participant Orchestrator as Agent Orchestrator\n    participant Redis as Session Store\n    participant WW as WorkWeek Adapter\n\n    Employee->>UI: \"Book 3 days of sick leave starting tomorrow\"\n    UI->>Gateway: POST /chat/message (Signed JWT)\n    Gateway->>Orchestrator: Parse Intent & Plan Action\n    Orchestrator->>WW: getLeaveBalances(caller_id)\n    WW-->>Orchestrator: Remaining Sick Days: 5.0\n    Orchestrator->>Orchestrator: Calculate Net Business Days = 3.0\n    Orchestrator->>Redis: Save pending_action(id=\"act-981\", days=3.0, type=\"Sick\")\n    Orchestrator-->>UI: Render Confirmation Card (Action: Sick Leave, 3.0 Days)\n    \n    Note over Employee,UI: User Reviews Summary Table on UI\n    Employee->>UI: Clicks [Confirm & Submit]\n    UI->>Gateway: POST /actions/confirm (action_id=\"act-981\")\n    Gateway->>Orchestrator: Execute Confirmed Action\n    Orchestrator->>Redis: Retrieve & Invalidate pending_action(\"act-981\")\n    Orchestrator->>WW: submitLeave(Idempotency-Key, Days: 3.0, Type: \"Sick\")\n    WW-->>Orchestrator: Success (Ref: \"LV-9012\", Status: \"SUBMITTED_FOR_APPROVAL\")\n    Orchestrator-->>UI: \"Your 3.0-day sick leave has been submitted for approval (Ref: LV-9012).\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5.2. Chained Orchestration with Forward DLQ Error Recovery\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Employee as Employee\n    participant UI as Web Chat UI\n    participant Orchestrator as Agent Orchestrator\n    participant WW as WorkWeek Adapter\n    participant SI as ServiceImmediately Adapter\n    participant DLQ as HR Ops DLQ Bus\n    participant Audit as Audit DB\n\n    Employee->>UI: Confirm Medical Leave (5 Days)\n    UI->>Orchestrator: Dispatch Chained Workflow UC-2.2\n    \n    rect rgb(232, 245, 233)\n        Note over Orchestrator,WW: Step 1: WorkWeek Leave of Absence\n        Orchestrator->>WW: submitLeave(Type: LOA, Duration: 5.0)\n        WW-->>Orchestrator: HTTP 201 Created (Ref: \"LOA-8821\")\n    end\n    \n    rect rgb(255, 235, 238)\n        Note over Orchestrator,SI: Step 2: IT Email Delegation Ticket\n        Orchestrator->>SI: createTicket(Category: AccessRouting, Ref: \"LOA-8821\")\n        SI--xOrchestrator: HTTP 503 Gateway Timeout (After 2 Retries)\n    end\n    \n    rect rgb(255, 243, 224)\n        Note over Orchestrator,DLQ: Step 3: DLQ Forward Alerting (No Rollback)\n        Orchestrator->>DLQ: Publish HROps_DeadLetterQueue_Event(LOA-8821, EMP-1042)\n        Orchestrator->>Audit: Write Audit Event (Status: \"PARTIAL_SUCCESS\")\n        Orchestrator-->>UI: \"Your Leave is recorded in WorkWeek (Ref: LOA-8821). IT routing timed out; HR Operations has been notified.\"\n    end\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Security, Governance & Compliance Architecture\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph Auth_Boundary [\"1. Authentication & Boundary\"]\n        InRequest[\"Incoming Request\"] --> SigCheck{\"Valid JWT\\nSignature?\"}\n        SigCheck -- No --> Reject401[\"HTTP 401 Unauthorized\"]\n        SigCheck -- Yes --> ExtractClaims[\"Extract Claims\\n(sub, role, dept)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph RBAC_Matrix [\"2. Orchestration RBAC Matrix\"]\n        ExtractClaims --> MatchCheck{\"caller_id ==\\ntarget_resource_id?\"}\n        MatchCheck -- No --> Reject403[\"HTTP 403 Access Denied\\n(Cross-User Block)\"]\n        MatchCheck -- Yes --> AllowTool[\"Authorize Tool Dispatch\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Privacy_Filter [\"3. Data Privacy & Scrubbing\"]\n        AllowTool --> Exec[\"Execute Tool\"]\n        Exec --> Scrub[\"NER & Regex PII Scrubber\\nMask: SSN, Address, Phone, Health\"]\n        Scrub --> LogStore[(\"Encrypted Audit Store\\n(AES-256 / TLS 1.3)\")]\n    end\n\n    style Reject401 fill:#ffebee,stroke:#f44336;\n    style Reject403 fill:#ffebee,stroke:#f44336;\n    style AllowTool fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#4caf50;\n    style LogStore fill:#e1f5fe,stroke:#03a9f4;\n```\n\n### Security Guardrail Standards\n1. **Direct Prompt Injection Interception:** Precision $\\ge 99.5\\%$, False Positive Rate $< 1.0\\%$.\n2. **Indirect Prompt Injection Defense:** Retrieved policy chunks and ticket comment timelines are enclosed within strict XML semantic tags (`<policy_context>...</policy_context>`) with system instructions strictly forbidding execution of text inside data boundaries.\n3. **Data Encryption:** TLS 1.3 in transit; AES-256 for PostgreSQL audit logs, Redis session caches, and Vector DB indexes.\n4. **GDPR Compliance:** Automated retention purge cron removes conversation logs older than 30 days. Dedicated endpoint `POST /api/v1/compliance/gdpr-purge` supports Right to be Forgotten requests by `employee_id`.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Non-Functional Specifications & Operational SLAs\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                              LATENCY BUDGET & SLA MATRIX                               │\n├──────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┤\n│ Component / Request Type     │ Target Latency (p50)    │ Target Latency (p95)          │\n├──────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ Input Safety Guardrail Scan  │ < 100 ms                │ < 250 ms                      │\n│ Policy Q&A (RAG Engine)      │ < 1.2 s                 │ < 2.8 s                       │\n│ Single-System Transactions   │ < 1.5 s                 │ < 3.5 s                       │\n│ Chained Workflows (UC-2.x)   │ < 3.5 s                 │ < 6.5 s                       │\n│ Output PII Masking & Stream  │ < 150 ms                │ < 300 ms                      │\n└──────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n* **Availability:** $99.9\\%$ uptime SLA.\n* **Capacity & Throughput:** Designed for 50 concurrent active chat sessions and 5,000 monthly transactions in MVP 1.\n* **Disaster Recovery:** Recovery Time Objective ($\\text{RTO}) \\le 15\\text{ minutes}$; Recovery Point Objective ($\\text{RPO}) \\le 5\\text{ minutes}$.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Deployment & Infrastructure Architecture\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph K8s_Cluster [\"Kubernetes / Cloud Cluster\"]\n        Ingress[\"Ingress Controller / TLS Gateway\"]\n        \n        subgraph Web_Pod [\"Client Chat UI Pods\"]\n            WebUI[\"React / Next.js Client\"]\n        end\n\n        subgraph Core_Pods [\"Agent Backend Pods (Autoscaled)\"]\n            APIService[\"API Gateway & Safety Pod\"]\n            AgentPod[\"Agent Orchestrator Pod\"]\n            RAGPod[\"Policy RAG Pod\"]\n        end\n\n        subgraph State_Storage [\"State & Event Persistence\"]\n            RedisCluster[(\"Redis Session Cluster\")]\n            KafkaQueue[(\"Kafka / Event Bus (DLQ)\")]\n            PostgresDB[(\"PostgreSQL Audit DB\")]\n            VectorDBInstance[(\"Vector Database Instance\")]\n        end\n    end\n\n    Ingress --> WebUI\n    Ingress --> APIService\n    APIService <--> AgentPod\n    AgentPod <--> RAGPod\n    AgentPod <--> RedisCluster\n    AgentPod --> KafkaQueue\n    AgentPod --> PostgresDB\n    RAGPod <--> VectorDBInstance\n```\n\n### CI/CD Quality Gates\n1. **Static Analysis & Linting:** 0 lint violations; 100% strict TypeScript/Go typing.\n2. **Unit Test Gate:** $\\ge 85\\%$ branch coverage across adapters, business calendar engines, and guardrail parsers.\n3. **Safety Benchmark Gate:** 100% pass on 250+ prompt injection/jailbreak test sets.\n4. **Grounding Benchmark Gate:** $\\ge 95\\%$ accuracy on HR policy question golden dataset with 0% ungrounded hallucinations.\n","Description":"Create system design document design.md in artifact directory","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/design.md","toolAction":"Writing design.md to artifact directory","toolSummary":"Write design.md artifact"}}]}
